-                                <h2 class="feature-banner-title">Deck Builder — generate, tweak, share.</h2>
-                                <p class="feature-banner-tagline">
-                                    Same Card Overview, with the Generate panel that turns the per-card averages into a tournament-accurate 60-card list. Eight buttons cover everything from "build it" to "ship it to a Discord chat".
-                                </p>
-                                <ul class="feature-banner-bullets is-keyed-to-hotspots">
-                                    <li><strong>Consistency</strong> — auto-generates the 60-card list from per-card avg-when-used. Math.round + Largest-Remainder + Reverse-LRM math; lands <em>exactly</em> on 60.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Max Rarity ↔ Low Rarity</strong> — flip every card to its highest- or lowest-rarity print in one click. Bidirectional toggle. Resets to Max on every fresh Generate.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Test Draw</strong> — opening-hand simulator. Draws 7 cards + tracks mulligans (<em>Basic in hand 77.8 % · Mulligan 22.2 %</em> in the screenshot).</li>
-                                    <li><strong>TCG Showdown ↗</strong> — copies the list and opens <code>tcg-showdown.com</code> in a new tab for full external playtesting.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Save</strong> — persists the build to your profile's <em>My Decks</em> with a name + format tag. Synced across devices.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Compare</strong> — side-by-side diff with another build (paste a list or pick a saved one). Colour-coded changes.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Deck → Proxy</strong> — sends the whole 60 to the Proxy Printer queue with one click. Sleeve and test.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Share</strong> — exports the built deck as a full-color PNG you can paste straight into Discord / Telegram / WhatsApp. No clipping, no link previews.</li>
