-                                <p class="feature-banner-tagline">
-                                    Format Staples ranks every card by <em>format-wide inclusion</em>: the percentage of <em>all</em> active deck entries that run at least one copy. Night Stretcher at 100 %, Lillie's at 97.1 %, and so on. This is the price of admission — if a card here drops below 80 % the format is shifting around it.
-                                </p>
-                                <ul class="feature-banner-bullets">
-                                    <li><strong>Inclusion %</strong> = <em>(decks running ≥ 1 copy) ÷ (total deck entries in window)</em>. Card-level, not archetype-level.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Tap any row</strong> → jumps to the Card Database entry with live Cardmarket price + every print + a wishlist hook.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>WR Δ on Climbers/Fallers</strong> — rolling 14-day matchup-win-rate change. A faller archetype with no card-pool change is usually getting teched against, not weakened structurally.</li>
-                                </ul>
-                                <div class="feature-banner-protip">
-                                    <strong>Pro tip:</strong> Cross-reference a falling archetype's drop with the Most-Used Cards list. If a staple in that archetype's typical engine slipped, you can usually point at the exact card that's failing the meta speed-check.
-                                </div>
