-                                <h2 class="feature-banner-title">The engine surfaces candidates — and tells you the WR Δ if you actually build with them.</h2>
-                                <p class="feature-banner-tagline">
-                                    Suggested Tech Cards are <em>candidates</em>, not commandments. Each card carries its threat tag (<code>RETREAT_LOCK</code>, <code>BENCH_DAMAGE</code>, <code>ABILITY_EX_IMMUNITY</code>, <code>ATTACK_IGNORES_EFFECTS</code>) so you understand exactly why it surfaced. You check the boxes you want and Build.
-                                </p>
-                                <ul class="feature-banner-bullets">
-                                    <li><strong>Where suggestions come from</strong> — the card-text capability engine scans every card's printed text and tags its interactions. Build vs… then intersects those tags with the threats your picked targets actually pose.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Threat tags on each card</strong> — labelled in blue next to each suggestion so the "why this card?" is right there. Surfer tagged <code>RETREAT_LOCK</code> against N's Zoroark; Shaymin tagged <code>BENCH_DAMAGE</code>.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Lock-in checkboxes</strong> — tick the cards you want forced into the next Generate. The button at the bottom updates to "Build with N cards" so you always know what you're committing.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Your Build vs Vanilla</strong> — same archetype, with vs without your tech overrides, weighted against the Meta Call field. <em>Vanilla 52.2 % → Your Build 52.8 %, Δ +0.6 pts</em>.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Per-opponent breakdown</strong> — the table at the bottom shows where the Δ actually came from. You see the +3 pts vs N's Zoroark and Dragapult Dusknoir come from the retreat-lock techs.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Estimator cap</strong> — Δ is hard-capped at +9 pts to keep claims honest; the per-card threat-bonus is <em>+3 pts per matched threat category</em>.</li>
-                                </ul>
-                                <div class="feature-banner-protip">
-                                    <strong>Pro tip:</strong> The detection log near the top (<em>"retreat_lock, surfer, switch"</em>) is the audit trail for the Δ. If a Δ feels too good, scan the log — sometimes a threat got double-counted and you can manually un-check one tech to recompute.
-                                </div>
