-                                    <li><strong>Beaten by — cards that defeat this</strong> — Card-Text Bypassers (e.g. <code>ABILITY_EX_IMMUNITY</code> attackers that bypass the target's ex-only protection) and Non-EX Attackers when the ability only blocks ex.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Good against — cards this one defeats</strong> — Specific Meta Matchups (Farigiraf ex, Pikachu ex, Sylveon) with HIGH / MED / LOW match strength from the capability-tag overlap.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>Capability tags</strong> — <code>ATTACK_IGNORES_EFFECTS</code>, <code>ABILITY_EX_IMMUNITY</code>, <code>RETREAT_LOCK</code>, <code>BENCH_DAMAGE</code> and more. Each one comes from a deterministic scan of the printed card text, not a community vote.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>+ Add missing tech</strong> — if you spot a card the engine missed, the button registers it as a local override. Stored in <code>localStorage</code> under <code>techLab.overrides.v1</code> — never leaves your browser.</li>
-                                    <li><strong>× Not a tech</strong> — same idea, opposite direction. Hide a candidate the engine surfaced if your testing confirms it doesn't actually help.</li>
-                                </ul>
-                                <div class="feature-banner-protip">
-                                    <strong>Pro tip:</strong> Local overrides are exactly that — local. Community rollout is planned for a follow-up release: aggregate confirmed overrides → ship them in the next data file → the engine learns from everybody. The more people use Tech Lab, the better the tech suggestions get for the whole community.
-                                </div>
-                            </div>
-                        </article>
-
-                        <aside class="tutorial-callout">
-                            <strong>The data file behind Tech Lab</strong>
-                            <p>Suggestions come from <code>data/card_capability_*.json</code> — a deterministic scan of every printed card's ability + attack text into a set of capability tags. The page reads those files at boot, applies your local overrides on top, then ranks suggestions for the picked target by tag-overlap strength.</p>
-                            <p>The roadmap: community overrides shipped in a follow-up release after they're aggregated and reviewed.</p>
-                        </aside>
-
-                        <aside class="tutorial-callout tutorial-callout--warn">
-                            <strong>When NOT to trust the Cooking suggestions</strong>
-                            <p>If the matchup matrix shows fewer than 30 logged games, treat the WR as directional. If your target's archetype was released within the past 7 days, the tag scan may not have caught all its interactions yet — open Tech Lab and use "+ Add missing tech" to fill the gap. If two of your three Build-vs… targets fall in the same threat category, expect Δ to over-report.</p>
-                            <p>The Cooking Promise: <em>the engine flags candidates; you still pick the build</em>.</p>
-                        </aside>
